test-jwt-private.pem / test-jwt-public.pem are TEST-ONLY keys, generated for this repository and
committed on purpose. Neither is a secret. The private half is still required: TestJwt signs a token
with it that no issuer in the system will accept, proving the resource server actually validates against
Keycloak rather than merely still accepting what it always accepted (see TestJwt). The public half is
currently unused — nothing reads it or points at it — left committed rather than deleted since deleting
an unused file that looks like it has a consumer is how the next person reintroduces one.
